    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d131-a1">

                <pb facs="0297" n="207" xml:id="pg207"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 69.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Knight to Mr.
                            Williams.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >New-chwang</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-10-06">6<hi rendition="#italic">th October</hi>,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 24.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi> A perusal of the inclosed copies of letters,
                    which I have the honor to hand yon, will explain a difference of opinion which I
                    have arrived at with the harbor-master of this port, in reference to the meaning
                    of clause 2 of regulation 7 of the pilotage Regulations.</p>
                <p>The question is one of great importance as regards the jurisdiction of this
                    consulate, and others as well; and, should you approve the stand I have taken, I
                    shall feel obliged if the harbor authorities of the port are so instructed.</p>
                <p>My dispatch to the harbor-master contains all I have to say on the subject while
                    the reading of the clause remains the same.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRANCIS P. KNIGHT.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. Williams</hi>, Esq., LL. D., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
